  "measurementTechnique": "Logical consistency: For C:N, biogenic silicate, CaCO3: subsamples of one sample, collected at P26, are analyzed with each set of data to check for continuity. Zooplankton that likely swam into the trap are removed. Silicate concentrations are compared to prepared standards.\n\nCompleteness: Dataset Complications: Some gaps in the data due to trap malfunction.\n\nProcessing step (1982): Data collected in collaboration with reasearchers at UBC.",
